// D1251 — a NUMERIC `as` CAST ON AN UN-ANNOTATED (hole) PARAMETER whose argument is
// union-repped. `vl check` returned 0 and the module was INVALID (`type mismatch: expected
// i32, found (ref $type)`): the cast emitted NOTHING, so the `{tag, payload}` box the call
// site pinned the slot to went straight into the i32 consumer. A clause-1 violation, and the
// annotated twin `function take(a: i32 | null)` printed 5 throughout.
//
// The checker solves an un-annotated parameter from its BODY, so a parameter only the CALL
// SITE pins keeps a `TyVar` — and `asExprIsUnionCast` read that. Closed 2026-09-03 by
// `asExprIsUnionCastIn`, which asks `exprUnion` (the emitter's own rep answer, and the
// monomorphizer's pin) where the recorded type is a hole. The `as?` spelling is a different
// mechanism, closed as D1341 by re-recording the cast's result at the call that pins the
// hole; the ARGUMENT delivery of that spelling is still open as D1371.
// Should print 5.
const u: i32 | null = 5

function take(a) { print(a as! i32) }

take(u)
